{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-sonnet-5-5","id":"msg_011CgkCbdbu7vSxUzfkXygUq","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"The contract is at `contract/claim.compact` and compiles cleanly (exit code 0). I didn't write or run any tests, so the claim logic is untested beyond compiling.\n\n- **`secretKey()`:** the only witness, with the type you specified.\n- **`publicKey(sk)`:** an exported pure circuit that returns `persistentHash([pad(32,\"claim:pk:\"), sk])`.\n- **`claim()`:** computes a nullifier from `secretKey()`, asserts it isn't already in the `nullifiers` set, inserts it, and calls `claims.increment(1)`. A second claim with the same key fails with \"Already claimed\".\n\n**Privacy:** the nullifier is hashed with a different domain tag (`\"claim:nf:\"`) from the public key (`\"claim:pk:\"`). Someone who knows a public key therefore can't compute the matching nullifier, and the ledger doesn't show whether that public key has claimed. I used a separate tag because storing the public key itself, or a hash that only a prefix change separates from it, would have let anyone look up a given user.\n\n**Disclosure:** the nullifier is explicitly disclosed with `disclose()`. The secret key never reaches the ledger.\n\nThe ledger fields are `nullifiers` (a `Set<Bytes<32>>`) and `claims` (a `Counter`). Both are exported."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":180,"cache_read_input_tokens":21619,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":180},"output_tokens":451,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c997f09b-9207-425a-ba5a-d75504c89bd2","uuid":"50233403-fbdd-4f21-9328-6063a0954394","timestamp":"2026-11-05T17:47:34.891Z","request_id":"req_011CgkCbdKXgxv7NrCS3t9PG